The diagnostic results suggest that the ANOVA assumptions are reasonably satisfied. The Shapiro-Wilk test gave a p-value of 0.111, so there is no strong evidence against normality of the residuals. Levene's test gave a p-value of 0.07542, so there is also no strong evidence that the group variances differ. Therefore, the ANOVA results appear to be appropriate for this dataset.
